WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.554 --> 00:00:01.819
- Growing up in poverty

00:00:01.819 --> 00:00:05.236
and mom was on welfare for over 10 years.

00:00:06.084 --> 00:00:10.019
But she never let any of that
affect her in a negative way.

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:10.996
Say you worry about a problem.

00:00:10.996 --> 00:00:12.539
So, here you are worrying
and all this stuff.

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:14.099
And all the sudden the problem's solved.

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:16.011
All that anguish for nothing.

00:00:16.011 --> 00:00:18.911
See, the physical application
of karate really is

00:00:18.911 --> 00:00:21.119
the smallest part of it.

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:23.095
And there's this one Indian
kid who just didn't like me.

00:00:23.095 --> 00:00:24.735
And everyday he'd chase
me home from school.

00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:26.472
I must have a direction for
me to get up in the morning.

00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:28.695
I got to know what it
is that I want to do.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.276
So, all four of us fight.

00:00:30.276 --> 00:00:32.487
My three students win and I lose.

00:00:32.487 --> 00:00:34.127
Anything you work toward,

00:00:34.127 --> 00:00:37.087
there are always obstacles in the way.

00:00:37.087 --> 00:00:40.591
- He's an american martial
artist, actor, and film producer.

00:00:40.591 --> 00:00:42.503
After serving in the
United States Air Force

00:00:42.503 --> 00:00:45.495
he began his rise to
fame as a martial artist.

00:00:45.495 --> 00:00:47.111
He appeared in a number of action films

00:00:47.111 --> 00:00:49.352
and had the starring role in the TV series

00:00:49.352 --> 00:00:51.127
Walker Texas Ranger.

00:00:51.127 --> 00:00:52.215
He's Chuck Norris

00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:56.382
and here's my take on his
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:58.414 --> 00:00:59.924
- Growing up in poverty

00:00:59.924 --> 00:01:03.645
and mom was on welfare for over ten years.

00:01:03.645 --> 00:01:08.269
But she never let any of that
affect her in a negative way.

00:01:08.269 --> 00:01:11.173
She always kept a very
positive image about life,

00:01:11.173 --> 00:01:14.405
saying that we may be poor
but we're rich in love.

00:01:14.405 --> 00:01:15.765
And I've always remembered that.

00:01:15.765 --> 00:01:17.406
And she's aways said that and always

00:01:17.406 --> 00:01:19.277
kept a positive attitude about life

00:01:19.277 --> 00:01:21.397
and that kind of carried off in me too.

00:01:21.397 --> 00:01:23.707
And I think that was some
of the success in my life,

00:01:23.707 --> 00:01:25.829
is I always kept a positive attitude about

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:28.173
whatever it was I was pursuing.

00:01:28.173 --> 00:01:30.805
Chuck Norris (chuckles).

00:01:30.805 --> 00:01:32.917
Chuck Norris' tears cure cancer.

00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:34.237
Too bad he never cries.

00:01:34.237 --> 00:01:35.603
Ever.

00:01:35.603 --> 00:01:37.695
(applauding)

00:01:37.695 --> 00:01:38.528
- Are you?

00:01:38.528 --> 00:01:39.397
Is that true?

00:01:39.397 --> 00:01:41.219
You don't worry about things?

00:01:41.219 --> 00:01:42.708
- No, because it doesn't do any good.

00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:44.227
'Cause the thing is, let's
say you worry about a problem.

00:01:44.227 --> 00:01:45.795
So, here you are worrying
and all this stuff.

00:01:45.795 --> 00:01:47.515
And all the sudden the problem is solved.

00:01:47.515 --> 00:01:49.411
All that anguish for nothing, you know?

00:01:49.411 --> 00:01:51.772
The thing is, worrying
doesn't solve the problem.

00:01:51.772 --> 00:01:53.355
It actually hinders the problem.

00:01:53.355 --> 00:01:54.403
What you've got to do,

00:01:54.403 --> 00:01:57.993
is try to find ways of
solving that solution.

00:01:57.993 --> 00:01:59.588
Or that problem.

00:01:59.588 --> 00:02:00.892
Finding the solution for the problem.

00:02:00.892 --> 00:02:04.381
And if you do, then you don't
have time to worry about it.

00:02:04.381 --> 00:02:05.420
- You're able to live by that?

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.540
- Well, believe me, I've, you know,

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.373
from the book, as you know,

00:02:08.373 --> 00:02:09.598
I've gone through a lot of ups and downs.

00:02:09.598 --> 00:02:11.654
The people see strictly my success.

00:02:11.654 --> 00:02:13.278
But they don't know where I came from.

00:02:13.278 --> 00:02:16.518
The kid who grew up in the
back hills of Oklahoma,

00:02:16.518 --> 00:02:18.854
who was totally non-athletic,

00:02:18.854 --> 00:02:21.118
and I won the world karate championship.

00:02:21.118 --> 00:02:23.174
And the kid who was
extremely shy in school,

00:02:23.174 --> 00:02:26.182
I'd never even done a high
school play or a book report,

00:02:26.182 --> 00:02:27.765
now I'm doing this.

00:02:30.113 --> 00:02:31.752
The thing is, you find formulas.

00:02:31.752 --> 00:02:33.824
You find things that will help you

00:02:33.824 --> 00:02:35.856
work toward what you want.

00:02:35.856 --> 00:02:38.335
Chuck Norris is currently suing NBC

00:02:38.335 --> 00:02:41.080
claiming Law and Order
are trademarked names

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.560
for his left and right legs.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.176
(laughing)

00:02:44.176 --> 00:02:45.093
- Last one!

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.733
Yes!

00:02:50.034 --> 00:02:52.202
- See, the physical application
of karate really is,

00:02:52.202 --> 00:02:54.452
is the smallest part of it.

00:02:55.306 --> 00:02:57.139
Most people think of Karate strictly as

00:02:57.139 --> 00:02:58.482
a physical application,

00:02:58.482 --> 00:03:01.906
but what it does for you
mentally, psychologically,

00:03:01.906 --> 00:03:03.915
and emotionally is much more important

00:03:03.915 --> 00:03:06.228
than what the physical attributes can be.

00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:10.403
For instance, we teach
success orientation.

00:03:10.403 --> 00:03:12.459
Positive-minded type goals.

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:14.771
Because many students
we get into our school

00:03:14.771 --> 00:03:18.283
come in there and they're very negative

00:03:18.283 --> 00:03:19.547
train of thought.

00:03:19.547 --> 00:03:20.380
"I can't do this.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.213
"I can't do that.

00:03:21.213 --> 00:03:22.259
"I can't accomplish things."

00:03:22.259 --> 00:03:23.787
And what we try to do as teachers,

00:03:23.787 --> 00:03:25.516
is to push out all the negative thoughts

00:03:25.516 --> 00:03:28.108
and replant positive
ideas of what you can do.

00:03:28.108 --> 00:03:29.988
What you can accomplish in life.

00:03:29.988 --> 00:03:31.875
And we set formulas, for them.

00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:34.083
Which, is very good, works
in all areas of life.

00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:37.011
Not strictly karate but
college training or whatever.

00:03:37.011 --> 00:03:40.428
And the formula that I emphasize is that,

00:03:42.182 --> 00:03:44.454
whatever goal you set for yourself,

00:03:44.454 --> 00:03:45.287
which we all do.

00:03:45.287 --> 00:03:46.991
As we get into the adult world,

00:03:46.991 --> 00:03:48.887
we all set goals for ourselves.

00:03:48.887 --> 00:03:51.463
The first thing you must have
is a mental image in your mind

00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:53.551
of what it is that you want to accomplish.

00:03:53.551 --> 00:03:54.407
Like, you're going to college now,

00:03:54.407 --> 00:03:55.567
you know what in your mind

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.687
of what it is that you want to achieve.

00:03:57.687 --> 00:03:59.711
Secondly, you must be determined

00:03:59.711 --> 00:04:01.951
and persistent enough to
stick with it long enough.

00:04:01.951 --> 00:04:02.855
Now this is where a lot of people fail

00:04:02.855 --> 00:04:04.415
because whether you're
going through college

00:04:04.415 --> 00:04:05.888
to get your master's or whatever,

00:04:05.888 --> 00:04:07.663
you're going to hit obstacles en route.

00:04:07.663 --> 00:04:09.142
You know, it gets tough at times.

00:04:09.142 --> 00:04:10.743
And a lot of times people will quit

00:04:10.743 --> 00:04:13.927
because of these obstacles in the way.

00:04:13.927 --> 00:04:15.391
And we always emphasize the fact that

00:04:15.391 --> 00:04:19.071
you must be determined to
overcome each obstacle en route.

00:04:19.071 --> 00:04:21.903
And that if you'll study, or
train, whatever it may be,

00:04:21.903 --> 00:04:23.615
accordingly there's not
a thing in the world

00:04:23.615 --> 00:04:24.527
that you cannot achieve.

00:04:24.527 --> 00:04:25.360
- [Interviewer] Yes.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.626
- This is one of my favorites here.

00:04:26.626 --> 00:04:28.481
When the boogeyman goes
to sleep every night,

00:04:28.481 --> 00:04:30.697
he checks his closet for Chuck Norris.

00:04:30.697 --> 00:04:34.639
(boisterous laughing)

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:38.374
- There is a scene in there
where you talked about

00:04:38.374 --> 00:04:40.957
bullies and running from danger

00:04:42.259 --> 00:04:44.068
and things like that when you
were trying to help this kid.

00:04:44.068 --> 00:04:44.901
- Yeah.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.395
What happens is this boy is being harassed

00:04:46.395 --> 00:04:48.043
by the neighborhood bully.

00:04:48.043 --> 00:04:49.917
And his father is encouraging his son

00:04:49.917 --> 00:04:51.923
to beat up this little boy.

00:04:51.923 --> 00:04:53.267
And I wrote this scene.

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.387
I wrote this particular
scene in the script.

00:04:55.387 --> 00:04:56.307
And I was trying to think,

00:04:56.307 --> 00:04:58.235
what can I write

00:04:58.235 --> 00:05:00.858
to encourage this boy to
handle this situation,

00:05:00.858 --> 00:05:03.283
you know, with this bully
in the neighborhood?

00:05:03.283 --> 00:05:05.411
And I'm spending days
trying to figure out,

00:05:05.411 --> 00:05:07.779
what can I say to boy?

00:05:07.779 --> 00:05:09.779
And finally I came up with the answer

00:05:09.779 --> 00:05:11.979
and it was a situation that I, as a child,

00:05:11.979 --> 00:05:13.810
had encountered, at about his age.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.909
I went to school in Arizona

00:05:15.909 --> 00:05:18.847
that was mostly Indians
from the reservation.

00:05:18.847 --> 00:05:21.259
And there was this one Indian
kid, who just, didn't like me.

00:05:21.259 --> 00:05:25.317
And every day he'd chase
me home from school.

00:05:25.317 --> 00:05:27.450
And I'd have to run by this gas station.

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:29.259
And this mechanic watched me being chased

00:05:29.259 --> 00:05:31.739
by this Indian kid every day.

00:05:31.739 --> 00:05:33.634
And finally he just
couldn't handle it anymore

00:05:33.634 --> 00:05:36.699
and he stopped me and
made me face this boy.

00:05:36.699 --> 00:05:41.145
And I told him, I said, you
know I told him I was scared

00:05:41.145 --> 00:05:42.104
and he says, well.

00:05:42.104 --> 00:05:44.232
And what he said to me,
which, is still true.

00:05:44.232 --> 00:05:45.520
Which, I remember.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.896
Is that, he says, "You know
that, running from your fear,

00:05:47.896 --> 00:05:50.080
"is more painful than facing it."

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.648
And that's something
I've always remembered.

00:05:51.648 --> 00:05:53.464
And this is what I relate to this boy.

00:05:53.464 --> 00:05:54.680
And of course eventually

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.880
he has to face this fear in the film.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.560
In fine print on the last page of

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.904
The Guinness Book of World Records,

00:06:00.904 --> 00:06:04.790
it notes that all world records
are held by Chuck Norris,

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.294
and those listed in the book

00:06:06.294 --> 00:06:09.254
are simply the closest
anyone else has ever gotten.

00:06:09.254 --> 00:06:10.366
- [Interviewer] Yeah, that's true.

00:06:10.366 --> 00:06:13.798
(audience applauding)

00:06:13.798 --> 00:06:15.622
- Again, you learn philosophies as you go.

00:06:15.622 --> 00:06:17.550
From experiences in life.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.790
You start learning philosophies and

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.190
things that will help you work.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.638
Like, for me, I'm very goal-oriented.

00:06:24.638 --> 00:06:27.022
I must have a direction for
me to get up in the morning.

00:06:27.022 --> 00:06:29.990
I've got to know what
it is that I want to do.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.894
And it's like when I was a karate fighter,

00:06:31.894 --> 00:06:33.526
all I wanted to do was run a local

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.614
karate tournament in L.A.

00:06:35.614 --> 00:06:37.102
But once I won it, I thought,

00:06:37.102 --> 00:06:38.511
well, how about the state title.

00:06:38.511 --> 00:06:40.678
So then the state title
became the next goal.

00:06:40.678 --> 00:06:41.590
And then when I won that,

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:43.598
there was national,
international, then the world.

00:06:43.598 --> 00:06:45.510
And if I would've said, "I
want to be the world champion."

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.062
when I first started fighting,

00:06:47.062 --> 00:06:49.030
it was too far beyond my conception.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.718
But I had realistic goals.

00:06:50.718 --> 00:06:52.814
Goals that I felt, in my
heart, I could achieve.

00:06:52.814 --> 00:06:55.283
The same thing in the movie business.

00:06:55.283 --> 00:06:57.538
You know, I had no idea
I'd be where I am today,

00:06:57.538 --> 00:06:58.954
- Sure
- when I first started.

00:06:58.954 --> 00:07:00.354
I just wanted to do a movie.

00:07:00.354 --> 00:07:03.106
Anything just to try
to get some experience.

00:07:03.106 --> 00:07:05.130
When Chuck Norris sends in his taxes,

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.706
he sends blank forms

00:07:06.706 --> 00:07:08.908
and includes only a picture of himself,

00:07:08.908 --> 00:07:10.978
crouched and ready to attack.

00:07:10.978 --> 00:07:13.146
Chuck Norris has never had to pay taxes.

00:07:13.146 --> 00:07:14.026
Ever.

00:07:14.026 --> 00:07:15.092
That's not true.

00:07:15.092 --> 00:07:16.338
That is not true.

00:07:16.338 --> 00:07:17.674
(audience laughs)

00:07:17.674 --> 00:07:19.354
My first tournament

00:07:19.354 --> 00:07:22.018
was in Salt Lake City, Utah.

00:07:22.018 --> 00:07:24.370
I take three of my students and myself,

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.034
we drive 16 hours to
get to Salt Lake City,

00:07:28.034 --> 00:07:30.074
to compete in this tournament.

00:07:30.074 --> 00:07:31.770
So, all four of us fight.

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:33.978
My three students win, and I lose.

00:07:33.978 --> 00:07:35.322
(audience laughs)

00:07:35.322 --> 00:07:38.236
So, I drive back while they
held the trophies, you know.

00:07:38.236 --> 00:07:41.955
But, you know, interesting how
philosophies are developed,

00:07:41.955 --> 00:07:43.452
because on the way back I'm thinking,

00:07:43.452 --> 00:07:45.844
well, what, how come I,
you know, I didn't win?

00:07:45.844 --> 00:07:48.772
What was it I did that made me lose?

00:07:48.772 --> 00:07:52.834
And so I started going
through the fight in my mind.

00:07:52.834 --> 00:07:56.622
And I said, "Okay, I
understand what I did wrong."

00:07:56.622 --> 00:08:00.230
And I said, "Okay, I may
make a mistake again,

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:02.214
"but I'm not going to
make the same mistake

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:04.126
"or the same loss again."

00:08:04.126 --> 00:08:06.614
And so, philosophies are
developed through this here,

00:08:06.614 --> 00:08:08.726
and as I tell my students, I said,

00:08:08.726 --> 00:08:10.974
"The only time you ever lose at anything,

00:08:10.974 --> 00:08:13.726
"is when you don't learn
from that experience.

00:08:13.726 --> 00:08:15.190
"'Cause that's what life is.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.664
Life is full of experiences
and if you learn from them,

00:08:17.664 --> 00:08:19.222
you're going to grow."

00:08:19.222 --> 00:08:21.168
Chuck Norris doesn't churn butter.

00:08:21.168 --> 00:08:22.718
He roundhouse kicks the cows

00:08:22.718 --> 00:08:24.278
and the butter comes straight out.

00:08:24.278 --> 00:08:26.054
(audience laughs)

00:08:26.054 --> 00:08:27.230
- [Interviewer] Now, is that real?

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.926
Is that for real?

00:08:28.926 --> 00:08:32.841
- Yeah, 'cause I have a ranch,
that's how I get my butter.

00:08:32.841 --> 00:08:34.554
Anything you work toward

00:08:34.554 --> 00:08:37.721
there are always obstacles in the way.

00:08:38.561 --> 00:08:41.354
And that's when you either
quit, or you continue on.

00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:43.458
And that's when I say,

00:08:43.458 --> 00:08:46.490
"To continue on, overcome that obstacle

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:47.666
"en route to your goal,

00:08:47.666 --> 00:08:51.282
"because you never know
which is the last obstacle

00:08:51.282 --> 00:08:53.551
"that's going to try to stop you.

00:08:53.551 --> 00:08:56.565
"And if you stop, that
could've been the last obstacle

00:08:56.565 --> 00:08:58.469
"en route to your success."

00:08:58.469 --> 00:09:01.233
Chuck Norris once shot
down a German fighter plane

00:09:01.233 --> 00:09:03.110
with his finger by yelling, "Bang!"

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.302
(boisterous laughing)

00:09:05.302 --> 00:09:06.812
- It's true, it's true.

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:09.312
(Chuck laughs)

00:09:09.312 --> 00:09:10.145
- Oh, man.

00:09:11.591 --> 00:09:13.266
- [Narrator] Chuck and
his team of Texas Rangers

00:09:13.266 --> 00:09:16.433
beat the bad guys from 1993 till 2000.

00:09:17.449 --> 00:09:20.825
- In fact, CBS wanted to go
another two years on the series

00:09:20.825 --> 00:09:23.103
and I probably would have considered that,

00:09:23.103 --> 00:09:25.949
except that my wife was
pregnant with our twins

00:09:25.949 --> 00:09:27.859
at that particular time.

00:09:27.859 --> 00:09:29.500
Towards the end of the eighth season

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.467
and I knew that I couldn't do a series

00:09:32.467 --> 00:09:34.295
and take care of my wife
during her pregnancy.

00:09:34.295 --> 00:09:38.084
So, I knew it was time
to call an end to it.

00:09:38.084 --> 00:09:41.216
Rather than being birthed
like a normal child,

00:09:41.216 --> 00:09:43.493
Chuck Norris instead
decided to push his way out,

00:09:43.493 --> 00:09:45.321
punch his way out, punch his way out.

00:09:45.321 --> 00:09:48.154
(audience cheers)

00:09:49.103 --> 00:09:50.572
It's like when I was a fighter,

00:09:50.572 --> 00:09:52.156
I'd be walking down the aisle to the ring,

00:09:52.156 --> 00:09:53.804
I'd be shaking hands and you know.

00:09:53.804 --> 00:09:55.655
And saying, "Hello" to everybody.

00:09:55.655 --> 00:09:57.602
But once I walked into the ring,

00:09:57.602 --> 00:09:58.692
my whole demeanor changed

00:09:58.692 --> 00:10:00.278
because there was a man across the ring

00:10:00.278 --> 00:10:01.906
who was going to knock my block off.

00:10:01.906 --> 00:10:03.491
And so, I had to change my attitude.

00:10:03.491 --> 00:10:05.319
I had to become much more aggressive

00:10:05.319 --> 00:10:08.531
and almost animalistic,
and when I fought him.

00:10:08.531 --> 00:10:09.914
After the fight was over,

00:10:09.914 --> 00:10:12.398
then I'd go back to a
more of a mild individual.

00:10:12.398 --> 00:10:14.307
And that's basically the
philosophy of my movies,

00:10:14.307 --> 00:10:17.250
the guy who isn't looking for
trouble, tries to avoid it.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:19.971
But when he's put in to position,
that he's got to face it,

00:10:19.971 --> 00:10:21.804
like we would have to do in real life,

00:10:21.804 --> 00:10:24.777
then he becomes that person
to deal with that situation.

00:10:24.777 --> 00:10:26.726
There are no steroids in baseball.

00:10:26.726 --> 00:10:28.756
Only players Chuck Norris has breathed on.

00:10:28.756 --> 00:10:32.043
(audience laughs)

00:10:32.043 --> 00:10:36.272
(hosts talking over each other)

00:10:36.272 --> 00:10:39.687
Believe me, these ought to
be screenplay writers here.

00:10:39.687 --> 00:10:42.137
The martial arts changed my whole life.

00:10:42.137 --> 00:10:44.619
I was a very shy kid growing up.

00:10:44.619 --> 00:10:48.786
And I was terrified to get up
in front of anyone and talk.

00:10:50.266 --> 00:10:51.570
All through high school,

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:54.089
I never once got in front of a class

00:10:54.089 --> 00:10:56.159
to give a book report or anything.

00:10:56.159 --> 00:10:58.312
When the teacher'd call me up and say,

00:10:58.312 --> 00:11:01.204
my real name was Carlos, by the way.

00:11:01.204 --> 00:11:02.665
But anyway, they'd get up and say,

00:11:02.665 --> 00:11:04.614
"Would you come up and
give a book report?"

00:11:04.614 --> 00:11:05.990
I'd be sitting at my desk

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.599
and I'd go.

00:11:07.599 --> 00:11:11.219
And my face would turn beat
red from embarrassment,

00:11:11.219 --> 00:11:13.836
but I thought if I got up
there I'd be more embarrassed.

00:11:13.836 --> 00:11:17.459
So, I went through that very
insecure time in my life.

00:11:17.459 --> 00:11:21.529
Then when I went to
Korea, at the age of 19

00:11:21.529 --> 00:11:25.513
and take my black belt and
I came back to the states,

00:11:25.513 --> 00:11:27.551
now I'm 22 years old

00:11:27.551 --> 00:11:30.112
and I'm stationed at March Air Force base

00:11:30.112 --> 00:11:32.144
in Riverside, California.

00:11:32.144 --> 00:11:35.437
And I thought, so, I was
doing my martial arts.

00:11:35.437 --> 00:11:39.623
Now, this is 1961-62 and
no one really knew anything

00:11:39.623 --> 00:11:41.896
about the martial arts at that time.

00:11:41.896 --> 00:11:44.458
And so I'm doing my kicks
and punches and all that.

00:11:44.458 --> 00:11:46.328
And all the GI's on
the base would watch me

00:11:46.328 --> 00:11:48.195
and they'd say, "Will you teach me that?

00:11:48.195 --> 00:11:50.194
"Teach us that stuff!"

00:11:50.194 --> 00:11:53.188
And I thought, well, maybe
I'll start a club on the base.

00:11:53.188 --> 00:11:55.749
So, I decided to give a demonstration

00:11:55.749 --> 00:11:57.696
at the gym on the base

00:11:57.696 --> 00:11:59.399
and I'll never forget this,

00:11:59.399 --> 00:12:01.802
this was 40-something years ago,

00:12:01.802 --> 00:12:04.936
and that night I was handing
out notices to everybody

00:12:04.936 --> 00:12:06.848
that I'm going to give a demonstration.

00:12:06.848 --> 00:12:09.935
And I thought, well, I'm
going to have to give a talk.

00:12:09.935 --> 00:12:13.380
And I'm 22 years old and I've
never done this in my life.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.471
So, I wrote out about
a half a page speech.

00:12:16.471 --> 00:12:18.263
And I memorized this thing for two weeks.

00:12:18.263 --> 00:12:21.430
I could say it forwards,
backwards, sideways, whatever.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:25.372
The night of the demonstration,
I walk into the gym

00:12:25.372 --> 00:12:28.015
and the microphone is lying on the floor.

00:12:28.015 --> 00:12:30.868
And I walk up, I pick up the microphone

00:12:30.868 --> 00:12:33.148
and I say, "Good evening,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:12:33.148 --> 00:12:34.654
"My name is Chuck Norris,

00:12:34.654 --> 00:12:37.625
"and I'd like to welcome
you here tonight."

00:12:37.625 --> 00:12:39.493
That's the last thing I remember.

00:12:39.493 --> 00:12:40.714
The next thing I remember,

00:12:40.714 --> 00:12:42.830
I'm walking out into the middle of the gym

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:45.516
to do my demonstration.

00:12:45.516 --> 00:12:48.115
And as I'm walking out
there, I'm thinking,

00:12:48.115 --> 00:12:50.033
did I finish my speech

00:12:50.033 --> 00:12:52.553
or did I just lay the microphone down?

00:12:52.553 --> 00:12:55.562
Well, to this day I
still don't really know.

00:12:55.562 --> 00:12:58.205
But what was important for me at that time

00:12:58.205 --> 00:13:00.872
it cracked the egg of insecurity

00:13:01.738 --> 00:13:03.889
that I'd carried around for 22 years.

00:13:03.889 --> 00:13:05.557
And then I kept forcing myself

00:13:05.557 --> 00:13:07.831
until that egg cracked open.

00:13:07.831 --> 00:13:12.282
And of course the results of
all that is becoming an actor.

00:13:12.282 --> 00:13:13.115
You know.

00:13:14.273 --> 00:13:16.428
Starting a foundation with Kickstart Kids

00:13:16.428 --> 00:13:18.629
which, is the love of my life now.

00:13:18.629 --> 00:13:21.790
I'm teaching the martial arts
in the inner city schools,

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:23.254
in the middle schools.

00:13:23.254 --> 00:13:25.612
Again, using the martial arts

00:13:25.612 --> 00:13:27.805
as a tool to help these kids

00:13:27.805 --> 00:13:29.719
develop the security in themselves

00:13:29.719 --> 00:13:31.630
that I lacked as a youngster

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.906
and helping them believe in themselves.

00:13:33.906 --> 00:13:36.353
That they can accomplish
anything they want

00:13:36.353 --> 00:13:37.855
in their life.

00:13:37.855 --> 00:13:39.276
If they're willing to
pay the price for it.

00:13:39.276 --> 00:13:42.119
And that's hard work and dedication.

00:13:42.119 --> 00:13:43.867
That's the secret

00:13:43.867 --> 00:13:46.345
to being successful in your life.

00:13:46.345 --> 00:13:48.948
And number 10 is, When
Chuck Norris does push-ups,

00:13:48.948 --> 00:13:50.496
he doesn't push himself up.

00:13:50.496 --> 00:13:51.923
He pushes the earth down.

00:13:51.923 --> 00:13:56.090
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:13:58.608 --> 00:14:00.149
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:00.149 --> 00:14:03.459
I made this video because
Zoh Gonzales asked me to.

00:14:03.459 --> 00:14:04.679
So, if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:14:04.679 --> 00:14:06.428
that you want me to profile next

00:14:06.428 --> 00:14:07.735
leave it in the comments below

00:14:07.735 --> 00:14:08.873
and I'll see what I can do.

00:14:08.873 --> 00:14:10.499
I'd also love to know
which of Chuck Norris'

00:14:10.499 --> 00:14:13.903
top 10 rules meant the
most to you and why.

00:14:13.903 --> 00:14:14.876
Leave it in the comments

00:14:14.876 --> 00:14:16.380
and I will join the discussion.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:17.840
Thank you so much for watching.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:19.303
Continue to believe.

00:14:19.303 --> 00:14:21.136
And I'll see you soon.

00:14:26.544 --> 00:14:27.377
(audience laughing)

00:14:27.377 --> 00:14:28.812
- So, you took acting classes and stuff?

00:14:28.812 --> 00:14:30.279
- Uh, yeah. Yeah.

00:14:30.279 --> 00:14:31.457
I took acting classes.

00:14:31.457 --> 00:14:33.494
Even in my acting classes
I couldn't get a part.

00:14:33.494 --> 00:14:34.636
- Oh my lord.
(laughing)

00:14:34.636 --> 00:14:35.469
That's...

00:14:36.508 --> 00:14:37.341
You're struggling.

00:14:37.341 --> 00:14:38.391
- That's the truth, that's the truth.

00:14:38.391 --> 00:14:39.569
Yeah.

00:14:39.569 --> 00:14:41.037
- Well, how'd you break through?

00:14:41.037 --> 00:14:41.870
- I don't know.

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:43.159
It just, determination.

00:14:43.159 --> 00:14:45.974
You know, and not giving
up and persistence.

00:14:45.974 --> 00:14:50.199
And I achieved the goals I
wanted in the karate world.

00:14:50.199 --> 00:14:53.007
I did, you know, in the
world title and my schools

00:14:53.007 --> 00:14:57.192
and I was trying to
decide what new energies,

00:14:57.192 --> 00:14:59.678
where I wanted to direct my energies at

00:14:59.678 --> 00:15:04.519
and Steve McQueen, who was one
of my students at the time,

00:15:04.519 --> 00:15:06.592
suggested the acting field

00:15:06.592 --> 00:15:08.394
and I just finished a movie with Bruce Lee

00:15:08.394 --> 00:15:09.819
called Return of The Dragon

00:15:09.819 --> 00:15:12.406
so I decided I would pursue that.

00:15:12.406 --> 00:15:14.128
Have you ever made a mistake?

00:15:14.128 --> 00:15:15.227
Of course you have.

00:15:15.227 --> 00:15:16.769
We all have.

00:15:16.769 --> 00:15:19.002
Many times it's hard to
face up to that mistake

00:15:19.002 --> 00:15:21.843
because it means you may
be laughed at or punished

00:15:21.843 --> 00:15:23.836
but when you do face up to your mistake

00:15:23.836 --> 00:15:25.908
and know that you'll never do it again,

00:15:25.908 --> 00:15:27.823
then you become a much stronger person.

00:15:27.823 --> 00:15:29.825
Here's my favorite one.

00:15:29.825 --> 00:15:33.554
They want to put Chuck
Norris' face on Mount Rushmore

00:15:33.554 --> 00:15:35.542
but the granite wasn't
hard enough for his beard.

00:15:35.542 --> 00:15:36.627
- [Presenter] Yes!!

00:15:36.627 --> 00:15:37.460
(cheering and laughing)

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.732
Got to applaud the effort, Chuck Norris!

